{"parentUuid":"9fe473c9-5cdd-44c3-9c55-fcb1bbab5482","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a67cf942cd679915d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ELCrtVKBiBDVrhDNNy4f3d","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"generalized totalizer encoding lazy decomposition pseudo-boolean MaxSAT 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Generalized Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints | Saurabh Joshi\",\"url\":\"https://sbjoshi.github.io/publication/gte-cp15/\"},{\"title\":\"Generalized Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-23219-5_15\"},{\"title\":\"[1507.05920] Generalized Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.05920\"},{\"title\":\"Mixed Radix Weight Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/8372038/\"},{\"title\":\"Encoding Linear Constraints into SAT Ignasi Ab´ıo1 and Peter J. Stuckey1,2\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp2014a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"dblp: Generalized Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints.\",\"url\":\"https://dblp.org/rec/journals/corr/0001MM15.html\"},{\"title\":\"Modulo Based CNF Encoding of Cardinality Constraints and Its Application to MaxSAT Solvers | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262209900_Modulo_Based_CNF_Encoding_of_Cardinality_Constraints_and_Its_Application_to_MaxSAT_Solvers\"},{\"title\":\"CMU CSD PhD Blog - Encoding Cardinality Constraints in Automated Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~csd-phd-blog/2024/cardinality-constraints/\"},{\"title\":\"Rethinking the Soft Conflict Pseudo Boolean Constraint on ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ijcai.org/proceedings/2024/0220.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT encodings for Pseudo-Boolean constraints together with at-most-one constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0004370221001557\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding generalized totalizer encoding, lazy decomposition, and pseudo-boolean MaxSAT:\n\n## Key Concepts Found\n\n**Generalized Totalizer Encoding (GTE):** GTE is an arc-consistency preserving extension of the Totalizer encoding to pseudo-Boolean constraints. This encoding is used to encode Pseudo-Boolean Constraints, and it led Open-WBO to win accolades in MaxSAT evaluations and Pseudo-Boolean evaluations.\n\n**Related Encodings:** Recent work has produced improved variants of the core concept. A more compact and efficient version of the popular Generalized Totalizer encoding was named Reduced Generalized Totalizer. Additionally, a new encoding called Reduced Generalized Generalized Totalizer (RGGT) first constructs a Generalized Generalized Totalizer (GGT) tree, then applies a reduction algorithm to obtain a more compact representation that replaces individual numeric values with intervals.\n\n**2024 MaxSAT Context:** While the original GTE work dates back to 2015, these encoding techniques remain relevant to modern MaxSAT solving. The search results include references to 2024 MaxSAT work, though specific details about lazy decomposition in connection with these encodings in 2024-2025 were not prominently featured in these particular results.\n\nThe search results do not specifically detail lazy decomposition techniques in connection with GTE for the 2024-2025 period, so you may want to search for more recent conference proceedings or papers from MaxSAT Evaluations 2024-2025 for the latest developments.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3eb7abe7-294b-4c5b-8201-7585cb777229","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:24.890Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9fe473c9-5cdd-44c3-9c55-fcb1bbab5482","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"18117db4-9d03-4d10-8a44-31def8849d9d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a67cf942cd679915d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mj5BXH4RwrVP7H37kjr72u","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT OnlyEnforceIf reification Boolean linear constraint propagation strength encoding\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Selecting SAT Encodings for Pseudo-Boolean and Linear Integer Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol235-cp2022/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 9: More Constraint Programming\",\"url\":\"https://www.cis.upenn.edu/~cis1890/files/Lecture9.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT encodings for Pseudo-Boolean constraints together with at-most-one constraints - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0004370221001557\"},{\"title\":\"Optimizing SAT Encodings for Arithmetic Constraints\",\"url\":\"http://www.picat-lang.org/papers/cp17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Encoding Linear Constraints into SAT Ignasi Ab´ıo1 and Peter J. Stuckey1,2\",\"url\":\"https://people.eng.unimelb.edu.au/pstuckey/papers/cp2014a.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"A Compact Encoding of Pseudo-Boolean Constraints into SAT | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-33347-7_10\"},{\"title\":\"Bugged reification of element constraint in CP-SAT? · Issue #1108 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1108\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here's what I found about these CP-SAT related concepts:\n\n## CP-SAT and OnlyEnforceIf\n\nCP-SAT's OnlyEnforceIf method means bool_var ⇒ constraint, implementing half-reification where instead of a full bidirectional constraint (b⇔c), it only supports (b⇒c). Half-reification involves a one-way linkage where the Boolean variable being True implies the constraint must be satisfied, but its being False does not necessarily indicate anything about the constraint's satisfaction, which is useful for expressing complex conditional logic.\n\n## Reification\n\nReification in constraint programming involves associating a Boolean variable with a constraint to capture its truth value, and full reification links a Boolean variable such that it is True if the constraint is satisfied and False otherwise. You can achieve full reification in CP-SAT by combining b⇒c and b⇒c (using OnlyEnforceIf with both the constraint and its negation).\n\n## Boolean Linear Constraint Propagation\n\nModern CP-SAT solvers achieve exceptional performance through integration with Boolean Satisfiability (SAT) solving techniques, creating a hybrid approach more powerful than either technique alone. Propagation is the process of using constraints to automatically eliminate values from domains through logical inference, where assigning one variable applies all constraints involving that variable to immediately remove values from other variables' domains.\n\n## Encoding Strength\n\nLinear and boolean constraints are generally most efficient in CP-SAT, whereas constraints like add_multiplication_equality can be significantly more resource-intensive. An encoding achieves GAC (Generalized Arc Consistency) if unit propagation of the SAT encoding results in solutions that correspond to the set of values after GAC has been enforced on the constraint.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3e2316dc-7686-4a6e-8012-4f58705d3ef0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:26.065Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"18117db4-9d03-4d10-8a44-31def8849d9d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
