{"parentUuid":"038c2897-cb8f-410f-95c9-0c8793eb9206","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a67cf942cd679915d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ep1JureeBgwZnbBP9NjYLp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" CP-SAT linear_propagation parameter boolean_encoding_use_native_propagator\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools/sat/linear_propagation.h Source File\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/cpp/linear__propagation_8h_source.html\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"SAT and Hybrid models of the Car Sequencing problem\",\"url\":\"https://siala.github.io/preprints/14-cpaior.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"Selecting SAT Encodings for Pseudo-Boolean and Linear Integer Constraints\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol235-cp2022/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38/LIPIcs.CP.2022.38.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OR-Tools CP-SAT parameters. There is a parameter `new_linear_propagation` (set to true by default) that controls linear propagation in CP-SAT.\n\nHowever, the specific parameters you mentioned - `linear_propagation` and `boolean_encoding_use_native_propagator` - do not appear in the search results I found. The search results reference the `sat_parameters.proto` file from the OR-Tools repository, which defines solver parameters, but the specific parameter names you're looking for aren't explicitly documented in these results.\n\nFor the most accurate and detailed information about these specific parameters, I'd recommend:\n1. Checking the official OR-Tools `sat_parameters.proto` file directly on GitHub\n2. Consulting the OR-Tools API documentation for CP-SAT solver parameters\n3. Examining the source code comments in the OR-Tools repository\n\nWould you like me to search for more specific information about these parameters?\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e04a26b3-22cb-4b99-9871-b2f2d11f22cd","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:49.303Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"038c2897-cb8f-410f-95c9-0c8793eb9206","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c35655c0-607d-4bae-aef7-357c54f2c277","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a67cf942cd679915d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017TnfPRKmns6ka4peYQYTJi","type":"tool_result","content":"# What the Author Says About Totalizer Encoding Efficiency\n\nThe blog post does **not** compare the totalizer encoding's propagation strength against sequential counters, BDDs, or sorting networks. The author focuses exclusively on the totalizer method itself.\n\nRegarding CDCL propagation, clause learning, or solve time differences, the author provides **no direct analysis**. The only empirical comparison mentioned involves Ed Wynn's work on bidirectional versus unidirectional clauses.\n\nThe author cites Wynn's finding that:\n\n> \"The effect of strengthening each encoding is small […] the lack of effect is much more surprising, because strengthening requires a substantial increase in the number of clauses\" \n\nHowever, this addresses encoding variants, not comparisons to other cardinality constraint methods.\n\n**The missing content:** The post concentrates on theoretical complexity bounds (establishing O(nu) clause counts) and implementation details rather than solver performance metrics across different encoding techniques. No benchmarks comparing solve times, propagation efficiency, or learning quality between totalizer and alternative approaches are provided."}]},"uuid":"46f37494-d2f4-435b-8243-0f81cfc3c9af","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:53.204Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c35655c0-607d-4bae-aef7-357c54f2c277","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
