{"parentUuid":"e7f2a4cd-7090-4521-8be1-b9e1a6628853","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a67cf942cd679915d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G8sDgG3QNFXdUQAk1tWsn3","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Abio Stuckey lazy decomposition cardinality SAT propagator generalize totalizer arc consistency 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"To Encode or to Propagate? The Best Choice for Each Constraint in SAT | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-40627-0_10\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] Encoding Linear Constraints into SAT | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/Encoding-Linear-Constraints-into-SAT-Ab%C3%ADo-Stuckey/1acfe0c039fb1ae06480e9f9efc5377c2240ee33\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict Directed Lazy Decomposition | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-33558-7_8\"},{\"title\":\"Conﬂict Directed Lazy Decomposition Ignasi Ab´ıo1 and Peter J. Stuckey2\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.upc.edu/~iabio/papers/lazy.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Conflict Directed Lazy Decomposition | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262289196_Conflict_Directed_Lazy_Decomposition\"},{\"title\":\"The totalizer cardinality constraint encoding for SAT | Blogarithm\",\"url\":\"https://www.curtisbright.com/bln/2024/12/31/the-totalizer-cardinality-constraint-encoding-for-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"Generalized Totalizer Encoding for Pseudo-Boolean Constraints | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-319-23219-5_15\"},{\"title\":\"CMU CSD PhD Blog - Encoding Cardinality Constraints in Automated Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~csd-phd-blog/2024/cardinality-constraints/\"},{\"title\":\"30th International Conference on Principles and Practice of Constraint Programming (CP 2024)\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/volume/LIPIcs-volume-307\"},{\"title\":\"Cardinality Constraints in Boolean Satisﬁability Solving Joseph E. Reeves\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~jereeves/research/jereeves_phd_csd_2025.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key findings related to your query about Abío, Stuckey, lazy decomposition, cardinality SAT propagators, and related concepts:\n\n## Lazy Decomposition and Cardinality Constraints\n\nAbío and Stuckey showed how to obtain the best of both worlds by lazily decomposing a complex constraint propagator using conflicts to direct it. Two competing approaches to handling complex constraints are: decompose the complex constraint into a set of clauses, or propagate the complex constraint using a standalone algorithm; the decomposition approach is prone to an explosion in size, while the propagation approach may require exponentially more search since it does not have access to intermediate literals for explanation.\n\n## The Lazy Decomposition Approach\n\nAbío and Stuckey proposed starting off with a full SMT approach and partially encoding, on the fly, only certain \"active\" parts of constraints. Their work extends the approach to reactively decompose Pseudo-Boolean constraints lazily during search; if the number of generated clauses during search exceeds a certain limit they decompose to a compact encoding using auxiliary variables.\n\n## Totalizer and Cardinality Constraints\n\nMany types of encodings for cardinality constraints introduce encoding variables that divide the cardinality constraint hierarchically into subproblems, with the totalizer being one of the most used cardinality constraint encodings, forming a tree-like structure.\n\n## Arc Consistency and Encoding\n\nRecent work introduces new CNF encodings of pseudo-Boolean constraints which allow unit propagation to maintain generalized arc consistency.\n\nThe search results did not return specific information about 2024 publications combining all these elements together. If you're looking for a specific 2024 paper, you may want to check conference proceedings from venues like CP 2024 or recent SAT conference proceedings.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0f50024b-a732-4eaf-858d-9a58ca3760cf","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:35.231Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e7f2a4cd-7090-4521-8be1-b9e1a6628853","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
